{
  "title": "Reinforcement Learning Fine-Tuning for Instruction Following and Math Reasoning",
  "authors": [
    "Yifu Han",
    "Geo Zhang"
  ],
  "year": 2025,
  "arxivId": "2506.21560",
  "abstract": "This study explores the effectiveness of reinforcement learning fine-tuning techniques on a compact language model for instruction following and mathematical reasoning tasks. The results show that preference-based optimization methods, such as Direct Preference Optimization and Reinforce Leave-One-Out, can significantly improve alignment with human feedback, even for lightweight language models.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "The study investigates how to fine-tune a compact language model using reinforcement learning techniques to improve its performance on instruction following and math reasoning tasks. <strong>Reinforcement learning</strong> is a type of machine learning where an agent learns to take actions in an environment to maximize a reward. In this case, the agent is the language model, and the environment is the task it's trying to solve. The goal is to find the best way to fine-tune the model to achieve high performance on these tasks.",
      "visualization": {
        "type": "flow-diagram",
        "description": "A flow diagram showing the reinforcement learning loop, where the language model takes actions (generates text), receives rewards (human feedback), and updates its policy to maximize the reward.",
