    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The study compares three fine-tuning techniques: supervised fine-tuning (SFT), Direct Preference Optimization (DPO), and Reinforce Leave-One-Out (RLOO). <strong>DPO</strong> uses a contrastive loss function to optimize the model's parameters, while <strong>RLOO</strong> uses a policy gradient method with a leave-one-out baseline to reduce variance in the gradient estimates. The study also explores the use of different reward models, such as DeBERTa and DistilBERT, to guide the fine-tuning process.",
